# The course as data

### How a folder becomes `tutors.json`

Week 1, Rung 1 of 7: Seed. Talk 2

---

## What rung 1 does

```
node src/main.ts ../fixtures/ladder-sample-course out/tutors.json
```

- reads a Tutors course **folder**
- writes one **`tutors.json`**: the course, its topics, units and sides, and every talk, lab, note, web link
  and archive inside them
- three source files, 244 lines, no dependencies, nothing to install

| File | Job |
| --- | --- |
| `src/model.ts` | the learning objects, as a discriminated union on `type` |
| `src/course-builder.ts` | walks the folder and builds each kind |
| `src/main.ts` | the command line |

---

## A course is a folder

The shared fixture, `variants/fixtures/ladder-sample-course`:

```
course.md                          <- the course's title and summary
properties.yaml
topic-01-basics/
  topic.md
  side-resources/
    side.md
    archive-1-solutions/   archive.md  archive.zip
  unit-1-intro/
    unit.md
    note-1-reading/        note.md
    talk-1-welcome/        talk.md  talk.marp
topic-02-practice/
  topic.md
  unit-1-lab/
    unit.md
    book-1-first-lab/      00.Lab-01-First-Steps.md  01.Setup.md  02.Build.md  img/main.png
    web-1-tutors/          web.md  weburl
```

---

## The folder's name is its kind

| Folder starts with | Kind (`type`) | Holds |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `topic` | `topic` | units, sides and learning objects |
| `unit`, `side` | `unit`, `side` | learning objects |
| `talk` | `talk` | a `.md` and usually a Marp deck |
| `book` or `lab` | `lab` | steps `00.Title.md`, `01.Title.md`, ... |
| `note` | `note` | one `.md` |
| `web` | `web` | a `.md` and a `weburl` file |
| `archive` | `archive` | a `.md` and a `.zip` |

A folder whose name starts with **no** kind is not content. It is left out, silently, with everything in it.
Upstream rule V002 is the validator's answer to that silence.

---

## Longest prefix first

`notebook-1` starts with `note`. It is still a notebook.

```ts
// variants/rung-1-seed/src/course-builder.ts
const kindsLongestFirst = [...folderKinds].sort(([a], [b]) => b.length - a.length);

export function folderKind(name: string): LoType | null | undefined {
  return kindsLongestFirst.find(([prefix]) => name.startsWith(prefix))?.[1];
}
```

Three answers: a `LoType`; `null` for a kind upstream builds and rung 1 skips; `undefined` for no kind.

Upstream: `findLastMatchingString` in `packages/jsr/gen/src/utils/file-utils.ts` sorts by length, longest
first; `getLoType` in `services/resource-builder.ts` turns `book` into `lab`.

---

## The prefixes are a table, not code

```ts
// variants/rung-1-seed/src/model.ts
export const folderKinds: [prefix: string, kind: LoType | null][] = [
  ["topic", "topic"], ["unit", "unit"], ["side", "side"], ["talk", "talk"],
  ["book", "lab"],    ["lab", "lab"],   ["note", "note"], ["web", "web"],
  ["archive", "archive"],
  ["notebook", null], ["github", null], ["tutorial", null], ["podcast", null],
  ["whiteboard", null], ["panelnote", null], ["paneltalk", null],
  ["panelvideo", null], ["quiz", null],
];
```

Upstream: `simpleTypes` and `loCompositeTypes` in `packages/jsr/model/src/types/type-utils.ts`.

---

## Title, summary, body

```ts
// variants/rung-1-seed/src/course-builder.ts
export function readMarkdown(file: string) {
  const contentMd = stripFrontMatter(readFileSync(file, "utf8"));
  const [first = "", ...rest] = contentMd.split("\n");
  const title = (first.startsWith("#") ? first.slice(1) : first).trim(); // upstream drops one "#" only
  const summary = rest.join("\n").trim().split("\n")[0]!.trim();
  return { title, summary, contentMd };
}
```

The first line is the title, the next non-blank line the summary. Upstream: `getMarkdown` in
`packages/jsr/gen/src/utils/lr-utils.ts`, with the `front-matter` package.

---

## What each kind holds

| Kind | Rung 1 reads | Upstream function in `course-builder.ts` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `talk` | a `.marp` deck replaces `contentMd` | `buildTalk` |
| `web` | `route` is the first line of `weburl` | `buildWeb` |
| `archive` | `archiveFile` is the `.zip` | `buildArchive` |
| `lab` | one `step` per `.md`, id from the file name | `buildLab` |
| `unit`, `side` | `route` points at the parent topic | `buildUnit`, `buildSide` |

A lab step `01.Setup.md` gets the id and `shortTitle` `Setup`: the text between the first and the last dot.

---

## An upstream quirk, kept on purpose

```ts
// variants/rung-1-seed/src/course-builder.ts, buildLab
// Upstream quirk: a lab with img/main.* takes the first step's short title as its own title.
const hasMainImage = folder.dirs.includes("img") && readdirSync(join(folder.path, "img")).some((f) => f.startsWith("main."));
if (hasMainImage && lab.los[0]) lab.title = lab.los[0].shortTitle;
```

So the fixture's lab is titled `Lab-01-First-Steps`, not `Objectives`. That is why every lab in this
module is named `00.Lab-NN-Title.md` and has an `img/main.png`.

Rung 1 copies the behaviour, not a better idea of it. The upstream oracle decides (week 2).

---

## Routes

```json
{ "type": "unit", "id": "unit-1-lab", "route": "/topic/{{COURSEURL}}/topic-02-practice/",
  "los": [
    { "type": "lab", "id": "book-1-first-lab", "title": "Lab-01-First-Steps",
      "route": "/lab/{{COURSEURL}}/topic-02-practice/unit-1-lab/book-1-first-lab",
      "los": [ { "type": "step", "id": "Setup", "title": "Setup",
                 "route": "/lab/{{COURSEURL}}/topic-02-practice/unit-1-lab/book-1-first-lab/Setup" } ] },
    { "type": "web", "id": "web-1-tutors", "title": "Tutors", "route": "https://tutors.dev" } ] }
```

`{{COURSEURL}}` is filled in by the reader. A web link's route is the external URL.

---

## Order inside a composite

Children are sorted by kind, then kept in folder-name order (a stable sort):

| `preOrder` | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 7 | 8 | 9 | 11 |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| kind | course | unit | side | topic | talk | lab | note | web | archive |

Upstream's `Map` in `type-utils.ts` fills the gaps: `tutorial` 5, `book` 6, `github` 10, the panel kinds
12 to 14, `podcast` 15, `notebook` 16, `whiteboard` 17, `quiz` 18.

---

## Upstream in one picture

```
course folder
   |  build(dir)              resource-builder.ts   a LearningResource per folder, typed by getLoType
   v
   |  pruneTree               resource-builder.ts   drops folders of kind "unknown"
   v
   |  buildCourse(lr)         course-builder.ts     buildLo, then composite or simple builders
   v
   |  generateDynamicCourse   tutors.ts             JSON.stringify into json/tutors.json
   v
json/tutors.json
```

Rung 1 folds the first three steps into one recursive walk: `buildLo` reads a folder and builds it.

---

## A first CLI

```ts
// variants/rung-1-seed/src/main.ts
const [courseArg, outArg] = process.argv.slice(2);
if (!courseArg) { process.stderr.write("usage: node src/main.ts <courseFolder> [outFile]\n"); process.exit(2); }
const courseFolder = resolve(courseArg);
if (!existsSync(join(courseFolder, "course.md"))) {
  process.stderr.write(`${courseFolder} has no course.md, so it is not a Tutors course.\n`);
  process.exit(1);
}
const outFile = resolve(outArg ?? join(courseFolder, "json", "tutors.json"));
const course = buildCourse(courseFolder);
```

Exit 2 for a usage error, 1 for "not a course", 0 for done. Only `main.ts` touches `process`.
Upstream `packages/jsr/tutors/main.ts` prints "Cannot locate course.md" and still exits 0.

---

## What rung 1 leaves out

- images, videos, PDFs, `frontMatter`, `hide`, `authLevel`
- `properties.yaml`, `calendar.yaml`, `enrollment.yaml` (they need a YAML parser)
- the kinds `notebook`, `github`, `tutorial`, `podcast`, `whiteboard`, the panel kinds and `quiz`:
  recognised, then skipped with a line on stderr
- Markdown to HTML: that is rung 2, week 3
- copying assets, `netlify.toml`, `llms.txt`, validation

Each is in `variants/rung-1-seed/RUNG.md`, "Deliberately left out". Week 2's assignment brings one kind back.

---

## Summary

- A course is a folder; a folder's name says its kind, longest prefix first
- Every learning object has a title, a summary, a body and a route
- Each kind adds what its folder holds: a deck, steps, a URL, a zip
- `tutors.json` is the whole course as one tree of data, written by a 23-line CLI

Read the note "The course format as data", then do Lab 1.
